# --- Captured data -----------------------------------------------------
# The tape is large and reproducible by re-capturing; it never goes in git.
data/
*.bin
*.tape
*.parquet
*.csv.gz

# The one exception: the small slices bundled for the notebooks, which have to
# be committed or the notebooks cannot execute from a clean checkout. The .tape
# is the first 100 blocks of a real capture — truncating on a block boundary
# leaves a completely valid file, which is one of the points notebook 02 makes.
!notebooks/sample_data/
!notebooks/sample_data/*.jsonl.gz
!notebooks/sample_data/*.tape
# Stage 6 bundles two tiny ONNX graphs and a sample of teacher logits so
# notebook 06 can show real quantisation scales and real soft targets without
# a checkpoint or a tape on disk. ~300 KiB total.
!notebooks/sample_data/*.onnx
!notebooks/sample_data/*.npz

# --- Model artifacts ---------------------------------------------------
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.ckpt

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Notebooks ---------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- C++ build ---------------------------------------------------------
inference_cpp/build/
*.o
*.so
*.dll
*.exe

# --- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Benchmarks --------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark *results* are committed on purpose: the README cites them, so
# they are evidence, not build output. Only scratch runs are ignored.
benchmarks/scratch/

# --- Stage 7 C++ ---------------------------------------------------------
# Build trees and the exported artefacts. Weights and fixtures are generated
# by `python -m ml.export_weights`; the fixture file alone is 16 MB of float32.
inference_cpp/build/
inference_cpp/artifacts/

# NOTE: a bare `docs/` sat here until Stage 7b and was silently excluding every
# interview-notes file and the benchmark methodology - all of which the README
# links to, and none of which had ever been committed. Removed. `git ls-files
# docs/` returning nothing is what surfaced it; a link check would have found it
# sooner.

docs/